.TE
.PP
A \f[CR]ref\f[R] views the bytes and holds their owner.
Nothing is copied.
The call passes a tag that it does not interpret.
.SS cbor::lazy::type
Gives the kind of the value at the lazy.
A tag 2 or 3 whose magnitude fits 64 bits gives
\f[CR]unsigned_integer\f[R] or \f[CR]negative_integer\f[R].
A larger bignum gives \f[CR]unsigned_bignum\f[R] or
\f[CR]negative_bignum\f[R].
A typed array (RFC 8746) gives \f[CR]typed_array\f[R].
Every other tag gives \f[CR]tag\f[R]; the call does not pass it.
.SS cbor::lazy::size
Gives the count of the head: the elements of an array, the pairs of a
map, or the elements of a typed array.
It reads only the head.
It does not read the children.
.SS cbor::lazy::empty
Gives \f[CR]true\f[R] when size gives 0, and \f[CR]false\f[R] when it
gives another count.
.SS cbor::lazy::elements
Gives the elements of an array, or of a typed array, as a view.
Each element of the view is a \f[CR]std::expected<lazy, error>\f[R].
The call reads only the head.
The view reads one element at each step.
.SS cbor::lazy::entries
Gives the pairs of a map, in the order of the bytes, as a view.
Each element of the view is a
\f[CR]std::expected<std::pair<lazy, lazy>, error>\f[R]: the key in
\f[CR]first\f[R], the value in \f[CR]second\f[R].
A key that occurs twice occurs twice in the view.
.SS cbor::lazy::clone
Decodes the whole item at the lazy into a tree of cbor::item, as
cbor::decode does.
The tree holds a copy of each text and byte string.
It does not view the bytes of the lazy, and stays valid after the lazy
and its owner end.
.SS cbor::lazy_elements
The elements of one array, from elements.
It is a forward range, a sized range and a borrowed range.
\f[CR]size()\f[R] gives the count of the head.
\f[CR]*it\f[R] gives the lazy of the element, or the error of the
element.
An iterator holds the owner of the bytes, so it stays valid after the
lazy and the view end.
\f[CR]front()\f[R] does not compile.
.SS cbor::lazy_entries
The pairs of one map, from entries, in the order of the bytes.
It is a forward range, a sized range and a borrowed range.
\f[CR]size()\f[R] gives the count of pairs in the head.
\f[CR]*it\f[R] gives the key in \f[CR]first\f[R] and the value in
\f[CR]second\f[R], or the error of the pair.
An iterator holds the owner of the bytes, so it stays valid after the
lazy and the view end.
\f[CR]front()\f[R] does not compile.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.SS cbor::lazy::at_path
Without \f[CR]T\f[R] it gives the lazy of the node.
With a scalar \f[CR]T\f[R] it reads the value as get does.
A text, a byte string and a typed array come back as a \f[CR]ref\f[R]
that holds the owner.
\f[CR]nodelist\f[R] gives every selected node.
The form with \f[CR]e\f[R] gives the result type of the query.
.SH ERRORS
.SS cbor::lazy
A lazy made with \f[CR]cbor::lazy{}\f[R] holds no top\-level item.
Each member function then throws \f[CR]std::logic_error\f[R].
.SS cbor::lazy::take_ownership
None from the bytes.
The call reads only the first head, to skip one tag 55799.
A step on the lazy reports broken input (at, get).
.SS cbor::lazy::view
None from the bytes.
The call reads only the first head, to skip one tag 55799.
A null \f[CR]owner\f[R] in the second form throws
\f[CR]std::logic_error\f[R].
An empty \f[CR]owner\f[R] in the first form throws
\f[CR]std::logic_error\f[R].
.SS cbor::lazy::at
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]key_not_found\f[R]: no pair has the key.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]index_out_of_bounds\f[R]: \f[CR]index\f[R] is not less than the
count.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]not_indexable\f[R]: a key on a value that is not a map, or an
index on a value that is not an array.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R], \f[CR]syntax_error\f[R],
\f[CR]indefinite_length\f[R]: the bytes up to the child are broken.
.SS cbor::lazy::operator[]
The errors of at.
.SS cbor::lazy::at_path
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]key_not_found\f[R], \f[CR]index_out_of_bounds\f[R],
\f[CR]not_indexable\f[R]: a step finds no node.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]incorrect_type\f[R], \f[CR]number_out_of_range\f[R]: the node does
not read as \f[CR]T\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]nesting_depth_exceeded\f[R]: the path is deeper than the limit.
.IP \(bu 2
A path that is not valid does not compile.
A path that can select more than one node does not compile, except with
\f[CR]nodelist\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
A query that is empty or moved from throws \f[CR]std::logic_error\f[R].
.SS cbor::lazy::get
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]incorrect_type\f[R]: the value is of another kind.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]number_out_of_range\f[R]: the number does not fit \f[CR]T\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R]: a string is longer than the bytes that are
left.
.SS cbor::lazy::type
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R] or \f[CR]syntax_error\f[R]: the head is
broken.
.SS cbor::lazy::size
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]not_indexable\f[R]: the value is not an array, a map or a typed
array.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R]: the count is larger than the bytes that are
left.
.SS cbor::lazy::empty
The errors of size.
.SS cbor::lazy::elements
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]not_indexable\f[R]: the value is not an array or a typed array.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]indefinite_length\f[R]: the array has an indefinite length.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R]: the count is larger than the bytes that are
left.
.SS cbor::lazy::entries
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]not_indexable\f[R]: the value is not a map.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]indefinite_length\f[R]: the map has an indefinite length.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R]: the count is larger than the bytes that are
left.
.SS cbor::lazy::clone
The errors of cbor::decode: \f[CR]too_little_data\f[R],
\f[CR]syntax_error\f[R], \f[CR]indefinite_length\f[R],
\f[CR]nesting_depth_exceeded\f[R] and others for a broken item.
.SS cbor::lazy_elements
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R] or another error of the bytes, when the
iterator cannot step over an element.
Each later position gives that error.
The view gives at most \f[CR]size()\f[R] values.
.SS cbor::lazy_entries
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R] or another error of the bytes, when the
iterator cannot step over a key or a value.
Each later position gives that error.
The view gives at most \f[CR]size()\f[R] values.
.SH NOTES
.SS cbor::lazy
A copy is O(1): one atomic increment of the owner.
No allocation.
.SS cbor::lazy::take_ownership
O(1).
One allocation: the owner, which holds the moved container.
.SS cbor::lazy::view
O(1).
No allocation: the lazy holds a copy of \f[CR]owner\f[R].
.SS cbor::lazy::at
A key: O(bytes up to the pair), at most O(bytes of the map).
An index: O(bytes before the element); O(1) in a typed array.
No allocation.
.SS cbor::lazy::operator[]
The cost of at.
.SS cbor::lazy::at_path
O(bytes before the target) for a singular path.
No allocation, except \f[CR]nodelist\f[R], which allocates the nodes.
.SS cbor::lazy::get
O(1).
O(bytes of the magnitude) for a bignum.
No allocation.
.SS cbor::lazy::type
O(1).
O(bytes of the magnitude) for a bignum.
No allocation.
.SS cbor::lazy::size
O(1).
No allocation.
.SS cbor::lazy::empty
O(1).
No allocation.
.SS cbor::lazy::elements
O(1).
No allocation.
A full loop is O(bytes of the array).
.SS cbor::lazy::entries
O(1).
No allocation.
A full loop is O(bytes of the map).
.SS cbor::lazy::clone
O(bytes of the item).
The tree takes one memory zone, which grows in chunks, and one
\f[CR]std::shared_ptr\f[R].
.SS cbor::lazy_elements
\f[CR]begin\f[R], \f[CR]end\f[R], \f[CR]size\f[R], \f[CR]*it\f[R]: O(1).
\f[CR]++it\f[R]: O(bytes of the element).
No allocation.
.SS cbor::lazy_entries
\f[CR]end\f[R], \f[CR]size\f[R], \f[CR]*it\f[R]: O(1).
\f[CR]begin\f[R]: O(bytes of the first key).
\f[CR]++it\f[R]: O(bytes of the value and of the next key).
No allocation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS cbor::lazy
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// bytes: a std::string with [1, 2]\f[R]
\f[B]auto\f[R] const doc = cbor::lazy::take_ownership(std::move(bytes));
cbor::lazy const copy = *doc;
use(copy.at(1)\->get<int>());   \f[I]// 2\f[R]
cbor::lazy{}.size();           \f[I]// throws std::logic_error\f[R]
.EE
.SS cbor::lazy::take_ownership
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// bytes: a std::string with {\(dqid\(dq: 42}\f[R]
\f[B]auto\f[R] const doc = cbor::lazy::take_ownership(std::move(bytes));
\f[B]if\f[R] (doc)
    use(doc\->at(\(dqid\(dq)\->get<std::int64_t>());   \f[I]// 42\f[R]
.EE
.SS cbor::lazy::view
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// owner: a std::shared_ptr<std::string const> with {\(dqid\(dq: 42}\f[R]
\f[B]auto\f[R] const doc = cbor::lazy::view(owner);
use(doc\->at(\(dqid\(dq)\->get<std::int64_t>());   \f[I]// 42\f[R]
.EE
.SS cbor::lazy::at
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// bytes: a std::string with {\(dqcars\(dq: [{\(dqhp\(dq: 5}, {\(dqhp\(dq: 7}], 7: \(dqseven\(dq}\f[R]
\f[B]auto\f[R] const doc = cbor::lazy::take_ownership(std::move(bytes));
doc\->at(\(dqcars\(dq)\->at(1)\->at(\(dqhp\(dq)\->get<int>();   \f[I]// 7\f[R]
doc\->at(cbor::key{7})\->get<std::string_view>(); \f[I]// a ref to \(dqseven\(dq\f[R]
doc\->at(\(dqbus\(dq).error();                         \f[I]// key_not_found\f[R]
doc\->at(0).error();                             \f[I]// not_indexable\f[R]
.EE
.SS cbor::lazy::operator[]
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// bytes: a std::string with {\(dqcars\(dq: [5, 7]}\f[R]
\f[B]auto\f[R] const doc = cbor::lazy::take_ownership(std::move(bytes));
(*(*doc)[\(dqcars\(dq])[1]\->get<int>();   \f[I]// 7\f[R]
(*doc)[\(dqbus\(dq].error();              \f[I]// key_not_found\f[R]
.EE
